   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ בֵּית שַׁמַּאי אוֹמְרִים: לֹא יָחֵם אָדָם חַמִּין לְרַגְלָיו אֶלָּא אִם כֵּן רְאוּיִין לִשְׁתִיָּה. וּבֵית הִלֵּל מַתִּירִין. עוֹשֶׂה אָדָם מְדוּרָה וּמִתְחַמֵּם כְּנֶגְדָּהּ.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «Beit Shammai say: A person may not heat water» on a Festival in order «to» wash «his feet unless it is» also «fit for drinking,» as they hold that kindling a fire on a Festival is permitted only for the sake of preparing food, but not for washing. «But Beit Hillel permit» one to kindle a fire on a Festival even for washing. «A person may kindle» a large «fire and warm himself at it.»"
  }
